      "message": "I see that we have to do the dance with errorData because this API method doesn\u0027t get the lock and we require it is held for `ConsumeError`. Could we have an issue to make ConsumedError threadsafe? We\u0027d only need to hold the lock in HandeError so the success case wouldn\u0027t need to get the lock. (no need to handle it in this CL stack, this is more to track improvements for multithreading)",
