      "writtenOn": "2025-09-29T19:04:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most of the dance here is to handle a couple separate things: \n * We now have this tri-state of A ShaderModule object that is valid/not valid (+error) and no ShaderModule (creationResult.IsError()). The old early-exit on success isn\u0027t as clean anymore.\n * Can\u0027t call the various Device error handling from a thread because error scope stacks are per-thread, the error would go to a worker thread\u0027s error scope and not be handled properly.\n \nBoth of these get much cleaner in future patches.",
